#+begin_comment
The simple method: this notebook holds only the headings org-scribe finds
things by. There is no template to fill in; what goes under each heading is
yours.

Add a character, a place, a plot thread, an object or a timeline event as a
heading directly under its section, and write whatever you like beneath it.
The capture commands do this for you, asking the same questions as in any
other method but filing no prose. A heading you
type by hand is recognised as well, once it carries a Role (characters), Type
(places, objects) or THREAD-TYPE (plot threads) property, which may be blank.

Keep the section headings as they are: org-scribe finds the entities by them.
Scratchpad is for anything that is not any of these yet. Nothing reads it.
#+end_comment

